{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>The nakedness of your father's daughter.</b> Some say she is the sister from [the same] father and mother, and we know that one who lies with her transgresses two prohibitions. Some say this verse is for reinforcement. The Sadducees said she is not his mother's daughter, and they interpret מולדת אביך (born of your father) as one whom your father raised. The meaning: the father took a wife and she had a young daughter; so too they interpret regarding Tamar. Their proof is: 'he will not withhold me from you' — only she was not born of David. And since the translators said that a father's wife's daughter is permitted, there is no need to respond against those who are certain in their own hearts. It is also possible that 'your father's wife's daughter' is the daughter of one who was raped."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:40.626406552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}